From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:42:48 +0900
Subject: Leave an inline trait's imports out of the classes which extend it

The statements of an inline trait are copied into each class which extends
it. A definition is given a new symbol and its body inlined; any other
statement is copied as it is, wrapped in an `Inlined` node. An import in the
trait's body is such a statement, and the node made for it has the type of
the import, which is not a type of a value: Erasure crashed on it, with
"MatchError: ImportType(Ident(Ordinals))", whenever the trait and a class
extending it were compiled in the same run.

The trait's body is typed before it is copied, so its imports have nothing
left to do, and they are now left out.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code); reviewed content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: inlinetraitimport
---
 .../src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inlines.scala |  4 ++++
 tests/pos/inline-trait-import.scala            | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/pos/inline-trait-import.scala

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inlines.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inlines.scala
index a4136eb4c5b65df255f2904b241e24661bd0f82d..4ca4f47dfe3de335e34e07fd2a0adc930daf881a 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inlines.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/inlines/Inlines.scala
@@ -996,6 +996,10 @@ object Inlines:
       val stats = Inlines.defsToInline(parentSym)
                          .filterNot(stat => overriddenDecls.contains(stat.symbol) && stat.symbol.is(Deferred))
                          .filterNot(stat => stat.isDef && stat.symbol.isClass) // Inline traits may not define inner classes; error elsewhere but skip now for best effort error msgs
+                         // An import has served its purpose once the trait's body is typed, and
+                         // has no place in the child: copied, it is an `Inlined` node whose type
+                         // is an import type, which cannot be erased.
+                         .filterNot(_.isInstanceOf[Import])
 
       val stats1 = stats.map{  // Private symbols must be entered before the RHSs are inlined
         case member: MemberDef => Left((member, inlinedSym(member.symbol, overriddenDecls)))
diff --git a/tests/pos/inline-trait-import.scala b/tests/pos/inline-trait-import.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1a14f2db7d6a3b87909e6f5a0d0ece549aab886d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos/inline-trait-import.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+//> using options -experimental -language:experimental.inlineTraits
+
+// An inline trait with an import in its body, and a class extending it in the same
+// run. The import was copied into the class with the trait's other statements, as an
+// `Inlined` node whose type is an import type, and Erasure crashed on it:
+// "MatchError: ImportType(Ident(Ordinals))".
+
+object Ordinals:
+  extension (index: Int) inline def twice: Int = index + index
+
+inline trait Counter[operand]:
+  import Ordinals.*
+
+  var count: Int = 1
+
+  def advance(): Unit = count = count.twice
+
+class Doubler extends Counter[Byte]
